        "original_id": "9b69e49c-359b-5186-9fa6-94195a5e41fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Bunte Blätter, Album for the Young\n- People: Robert Schumann, Friedrich Wieck\n- Roles: composer, music critic, pianist, teacher\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Schumann was born on 8 June 1810 and died on 29 July 1856.\n- Robert Schumann was a German composer and an influential music critic.\n- Friedrich Wieck was Robert Schumann's teacher.\n- Friedrich Wieck told Robert Schumann that he could become the finest pianist in Europe.\n- A hand injury ended Robert Schumann's dream of becoming a leading pianist.\n- Bunte Blätter, Op. 99, is a collection of piano pieces by Robert Schumann.\n- Robert Schumann assembled Bunte Blätter from earlier unpublished pieces after the success of Album for the Young.",
